<title>SOUTH AFRICA: US says Iscor, Hiveld dumping -paper.</title>
<headline>US says Iscor, Hiveld dumping -paper.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. commerce department has issued a preliminary finding that Iscor Ltd and Highveld Steel and Vanadium Corp Ltd have been dumping cut-to-length carbon steel plates in the U.S. market, Business Day said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dumping duties of 31 percent and 16 percent have been assessed on the products of Iscor and Hiveld respectively, reflecting the difference between the lower U.S. and higher domestic prices of the firms, adjusted for transport and other costs, it said.</p>
<p>The duties will go into effect in the next few days when the finding is published in the government gazette.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
